<title>USA: U.S. weekend box office chart -- May 2-4.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekend box office chart -- May 2-4.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the May 2-4 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. Breakdown		  $12,307,128	 $  ----</p>
<p>2. Austin Powers:</p>
<p>    International Man</p>
<p>    of Mystery		$ 9,548,111	 $  ----</p>
<p>3. Volcano		    $ 9,099,743	 $ 27,443,779</p>
<p>4. Liar Liar		  $ 5,858,255	 $151,487,405</p>
<p>5. Romy and Michele's</p>
<p>    High School Reunion   $ 5,326,806	 $ 14,858,363</p>
<p>6. Anaconda		   $ 4,720,202	 $ 49,456,213</p>
<p>7. Warriors of Virtue     $ 3,277,084	 $  ----</p>
<p>8. The Saint		  $ 3,061,024	 $ 52,496,506</p>
<p>9. Murder at 1600	   $ 2,845,827	 $ 19,530,609</p>
<p>10 Grosse Pointe Blank    $ 2,051,361	 $ 21,121,291</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Breakdown&quot; and &quot;The Saint&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner Inc. Time Warner's Warner Bros. released &quot;Murder at 1600.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Volcano&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;Liar Liar&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;Romy and Michele's High School Reunion&quot; and &quot;Grosse Pointe Blank&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co</p>
<p>&quot;Anaconda&quot; is released by Sony Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;Warriors of Virtue&quot; is released by MGM, which is owned by Kirk Kerkorian and Australia's Seven Network Ltd</p>
</text>
